          "kicker": "Structural crisis",
          "heading": "Scarlets and Ospreys fight WRU over proposed professional team cut",
          "body": "The future of regional rugby in west Wales remains under intense scrutiny as Scarlets and Ospreys contest the Welsh Rugby Union’s plan to scrap one of the four professional teams by 2028. While Cardiff and Dragons have been identified as safe, the remaining two sides are now fighting for survival. Scarlets director of rugby Nigel Davies described the WRU's shifting long-term strategy as \"chaos,\" noting that it would be \"unacceptable in any other walk of life\" to plan so inconsistently."
