          "kicker": "Selection concern",
          "heading": "Len Ikitau faces fitness wait as Wallabies midfield options dwindle",
          "body": "Australia’s midfield plans for the Bledisloe Cup have hit an early hurdle following Sunday’s victory over the Springboks. Two-try hero Len Ikitau is managing an ankle injury, with head coach Les Kiss labelling the status “precautionary.” Meanwhile, centre partner Hunter Paisami faces a disciplinary hearing today following a high tackle citation. Kiss, who remains undefeated, is exploring tactical flexibility, noting that Joseph-Aukuso Suaalii could provide cover in the centres or at full-back if further rotation is required."
        }
