          "heading": "Fehi Fineanganofo re-signs with New Zealand Rugby until end of 2027",
          "body": "Winger Fehi Fineanganofo will remain in New Zealand for an additional season after negotiating an exit from his Newcastle Red Bulls deal. The 24-year-old, who broke the Hurricanes' single-season try-scoring record this year, will now continue his career in Super Rugby Pacific through 2027 to prioritise his international ambitions. New Zealand Rugby and the English club reached a collaborative agreement, allowing the All Black to chase selection for next year’s World Cup before his eventual move to the Premiership."
