      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Selection scrutiny",
          "heading": "Nick Mallett questions Rassie Erasmus' selection: 'He looks like a lock'",
          "body": "Former Springboks head coach Nick Mallett has criticised Rassie Erasmus’ selection following the 42-38 defeat to the Wallabies in Perth. Mallett questioned the back-row balance, specifically suggesting that Elrigh Louw “looks more like a lock playing flank as opposed to a proper out-and-out flank who's really quick.” While acknowledging the team’s depth, Mallett argued that the match was not of sufficient importance to warrant 13 changes, noting that South Africa trailed by as many as 25 points during the second half."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Planet Rugby"
